\f1\fs22 Monday morning arrived and, as the virtuously privileged consumed their news and opinion\'97while breakfasting on poached eggs, wild-caught salmon, artisanal sourdough toast, and tea brewed from those leaves they bought years ago while trekking the wheelchair-access foothills of the Himalayas\'97they wondered what the tax had happened on the Lord\'92s day while they were praying for righteous profit margins. \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Dunhilton\'92s spin surgeons advised him to address the nation, and quickly improvised a press conference to be streamed live on the UBC and pantomimed later on the more trustworthy commercial broadcasters during the pre-footy news.\
On the plaza they rearranged couches and propped tablets on stacks of eskies. By the time the salamander face of Piotr Dunhilton composed itself before the crest of the Airborne Meritocracy of Ulyssia (which depicted a solemn kangaroo and startled emu watching a solemn scene of turning back boats) the Get Bent crowd has settled down for the show and was sharing caramelised popcorn dripping in melted pork fat.\
\'93My fellow Airborne Ulyssians,\'94 Dunhilton began. \'93You did not build your towers so that just anyone could stand underneath them.\'94\
Everyone on the plaza stood up and cheered.\
\'93What you are seeing on Bent Street is not a protest. Let me speak plainly to decent people: it is loitering, with a sound system. It is a confederation of the institutionally disentitled, the professionally idle. They are nothing but not-for-profit terrorists, and failed buskers.\'94 He paused there, trying to be statesmanlike, and ended up looking like a croupier in an illegal casino. \'93And it grieves me to report that among them stand a number of impressionable children of decent shareholding families, groomed during a seditiously free concert on The Domain that was mischaracterised as a classical music to unlawfully secure permission. Our children were bribed with gifts of free guitars, and were forced to  consume toxic alcoholic drinks and mind-altering drugs. They were brainwashed with slogans and hypnotic chants, and encouraged by cult leaders to take part in not-for-profit rituals, including the  consumption of free sausages.\'94\
On the plaza, the Airborne kids cheered. One shouted, \'93My dad paid for those sausages.\'94\
Dunhilton continued. \'93To the decent, deserving people of this city I say: your government will not reward attention-seeking with attention. There are true Ulyssians\'97those who have honoured their inheritances and lawfully grifted their rewards\'97and then there are the others. There are Ulyssians, and there are occupants, those that immigrated too late of have been squatting for free since the dawn of time. It is these others that have desecrated the day of rest, the day of Latter Day Capitalist saints,  when they should be cleaning our bathrooms, laundering our clothes, waiting on our tables, and\'97I must say this\'97they must stop wingeing about the lawful tax on adult diapers.\'94\
\'93Someone should put a diaper on that man\'92s head,\'94 said some on the plaza. The laughter and responses drowned out some of the diaper-collectibles coming out Dunhilton\'92s mouth.\
\'93I have therefore ordered TRAMPS riot squads into the precinct. Their mission is twofold. One: to rescue all Airborne hostages; two: send the undeserving back under the filth they created by their lack of enterprise and breeding; three: throw the fomenters in jail for not less than a term of seven generations; and four: restore our beloved above-Layer city to normal for freedom-loving Ulyssians everywhere.\'94\
The crowd on the plaza booed, none louder than the Airborne kids.\
\'93They\'92re teaching us to play guitar, you chimpanzee!\'94 one of them shouted to a tablet they were watching.\
Dunhilton finished and asked the press scrum for questions. They were allowed three. Asked when the plaza would be cleared, Dunhilton said that timelines were commercially confidential. Asked whether the government would negotiate, he said that you do not negotiate with a picnic. And asked\'97by a young journalist who had not been at the Daily Smear long enough to know better\'97whether the presence of so many shareholders\'92 children made a clearance operation politically inadvisable, Dunhilton looked at her for a long, amphibious moment and announced that the briefing had run to time.\
By the evening bulletins the occupation led every channel, with pictures from hover-copts  of the crowd Nobody agreed on how many people were on the plaza, since every channel counted with its owner\'92s thumb on the scale. UBC reported as many as fifteen thousand people occupied the plaza, almost half of them Airborne. Channel Slime News found almost thirty thousand Elvi and Cloudborne activists, the Airborne having vanished from its arithmetic entirely. And Sty News reported in excess of fifty thousand not-for-profit terrorists, which was arithmetically beyond the forty thousand it was estimated the plaza could hold at a complete crush.\
Blake Mudrake of Channel Sty News managed to get a camera crew onto the plaza. Unfortunately, all the footage he got had to be consigned to a bonfire of wage agreement contracts, mostly because almost of all of it showed Airborne kids in the background having an exceptionally fun time. Later footage showed Blake Mudrake himself out of his TV-personality mind, playing air guitar, karate kicking and singing, \'93Praise the Dawkins, he\'92s the one.\'94 His lawyers had always planned to argue that he was drugged without his knowledge, but the matter was never heard in court, mostly because Mudrake quit his job and became a non-for-profit terrorist.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

