\f1\fs22 None of the news coverage mentioned the riot squads that Dunhilton promised. They arrived on dusk and were unexpectedly repelled by an impenetrable perimeter of Airborne kids sitting in couches. It was not so much the configuration of couches that repelled as much as it was the kids laughing at them. No TRAMPS officer that had checked the box marked 
\fs20 RIOT SQUAD
\fs22  as a career option signed up for this. They had not been given the training and, because they had not been trained, they had no clue what to do. The kids offered them fried peanut butter and banana sandwiches; they offered them fool\'92s gold. Some of the Riot Squad took the offerings. Some of 
\f2\i those
\f1\i0  put down their armaments and shields, and took off their flak jackets, and joined the party.
\fs26 \
